; One stage of the upsampler: a phase of a polyphase FIR filter, a tap at a time, its sum put out at the phase's end.
; Each tap reads a sample x, then five cards from words that are its coefficient as instructions, straight into the
; routine, as a lattice machine reads reduce's: the sign word (ADD t or SUB t), the word for the coefficient's third
; digit, the jumps into the row of nine ADDs for its second and first digits (or SFT 00 for a 0), and the jump to
; the next tap or to the routine that puts the sum out.
;
; A tap's product is c x times 10, in tenths of a unit, for c = 0.d1 d2 d3: Horner from the last digit, d3 v, SFT 01,
; + d2 v, SFT 01, + d1 v, with v = +x or -x in the row's cell c (each SFT truncating towards zero). The accumulator
; holds v after the sign word, so the third digit's word is CLA z for 0, nothing for 1, and d3 - 1 ADDs otherwise.
; The sum S can pass a card, so it is kept as thousands and units, hi and lo, with the sign each happens to have;
; STO keeps the units of P + lo and SFT 03 gives the carry. The row is cells 90-98, and it runs on into cell 99,
; which holds the way back that the JMP into it left there.
;
; Stage 1 (16 kHz) puts S / 10 out as one card, rounded half away from zero; stage 2 (48 kHz) puts the sample 2 S
; out (S is in tenths of yd, and the sample is 20 yd) as its thousands and then its units from 0 to 999, as the
; output stage does: 2 S's units summed on top of 2000, so they never go negative. The 16 kHz sample that is a 48 kHz
; sample itself comes as a tap whose words are ADD t and three SFT 10, ten times the sample.
;
; Address Contents Label Opcode Operand Comment
  03            tap     INP   t        03-22: one tap, S = S + 10 c x
  04                    INP   sw
  05                    INP   j3
  06                    INP   j2
  07                    INP   j1
  08                    INP   nx
  09                    CLA   z
  10            sw      DATA  0        (ADD t or SUB t)
  11                    STO   c
  12            j3      DATA  0        (CLA z, SFT 00, or JMP into the row for d3 - 1 ADDs)
  13                    SFT   01
  14            j2      DATA  0        (SFT 00, or JMP into the row for d2 ADDs)
  15                    SFT   01
  16            j1      DATA  0        (SFT 00, or JMP into the row for d1 ADDs)
  17                    ADD   lo
  18                    STO   lo
  19                    SFT   03
  20                    ADD   hi
  21                    STO   hi
  22            nx      DATA  0        (JMP tap, or JMP one or pair)
  23            one     CLA   hi       23-37: stage 1, S / 10 rounded out
  24                    SFT   30
  25                    ADD   lo
  26                    TAC   neg
  27                    ADD   five
  28                    SFT   01
  29                    JMP   put
  30            neg     SUB   five
  31                    SFT   01
  32            put     STO   y
  33                    OUT   y
  34                    CLA   z
  35                    STO   lo
  36                    STO   hi
  37                    JMP   tap
  38            pair    CLA   two      38-53: stage 2, 2 S out as thousands and units
  39                    SFT   30
  40                    ADD   lo
  41                    ADD   lo
  42                    STO   u
  43                    SFT   03
  44                    ADD   hi
  45                    ADD   hi
  46                    SUB   two
  47                    STO   y
  48                    OUT   y
  49                    OUT   u
  50                    CLA   z
  51                    STO   lo
  52                    STO   hi
  53                    JMP   tap
  54            t       DATA  0        t and z are where words expects them
  55            lo      DATA  0
  56            hi      DATA  0
  57            y       DATA  0
  58            u       DATA  0
  59            z       DATA  0
  60            five    DATA  5
  61            two     DATA  2
  89            c       DATA  0
  90            row     ADD   c        90-98: the row of nine ADDs, into 99
  91                    ADD   c
  92                    ADD   c
  93                    ADD   c
  94                    ADD   c
  95                    ADD   c
  96                    ADD   c
  97                    ADD   c
  98                    ADD   c
